    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Mortal year Gu sit below ten years, including one year Gu, two year Gu, and five year Gu. Year Gu at rank six are at least ten years and unique in the world. A ten year immortal level year Gu can be raised with immortal materials into higher year counts up to ninety-nine year Gu. Hundred year Gu is rank seven, and raising ten year Gu to hundred year Gu is ordinary rank-up refinement rather than parallel refinement. Thousand year Gu is rank eight; ten thousand year Gu would be rank nine in theory, but history has never had one, while rank eight thousand year Gu has existed.",
        "chapters": [
          1129
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-of-use-and-food",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "A fifty year Gu can become a twenty year Gu after one use. If a thousand year Gu falls to nine hundred year Gu, it drops from rank eight to rank seven. Strictly speaking it is a consumable Immortal Gu, but not a one-time consumable: it can be expended and then replenished again. It feeds on the water of the River of Time, the same food as Spring Autumn Cicada.",
        "chapters": [
          1129
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-of-use-and-food",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_river_of_time",
          "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
